A||N||4||Deicide||5 speed transmission||||1||
Z||000000||Deicide||10-30-2000||10:36 PM||||I might be buying an '86 Fiero 4 cylinder, but I am planning to put a supermodified 2.8 6 cylinder in its place.  I was wondering if the 5 speed used on the 4 cylinder is the same used on the 6.<P>Also just out of curiosity, what is the 0-60 time for the 2.5L Fiero w/ the 5 speed?<P>Thanks.<BR><P>------------------<BR>--Deicide||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||10-30-2000||10:59 PM||||4 cyl uses Izuzu tranny, v-6 uses Getrag. They are different.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Bob Englert||10-30-2000||11:00 PM||||All 5sp transmissions used in 4 cyl Fieros were made by Isuzu and are generally considered weaker that the Getrag 5sp used in the v6 Fieros.<P>The Fiero originally came with a 4 sp transmission in 84 with the 4 cyl.  This transmission was continued with the v6 motors beginning in 85 and most of 86.  The Getrag 5sp was introduced near the end of the 86 model run for the v6 cars and was continued through the end of production in 88.<P>The Isuzu 5sp was introduced for the 4cyl cars in 85 and continued in the 4 cyl cars through the end of production in 88.  <P>Some have used the Isuzu with the v6, but I think there are some compatibility issues with clutch size, etc.  The Isuzu was not intended for the higher torque and HP that the v6 produces.  <P>If you want to drop the clutch with reckless abandon, get a 4sp trans.  I hear they are very strong and cheap compared to the Getrags.<P>Bob<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||10-30-2000||11:09 PM||||I agree with the above comments, based only upon my personal opinion that if GM could have used the Isuzu with the V6's, they <B>would</B> have.  But they didn't!<P>BTW, to answer your second question, the 0-60 time for the 2.5-l + 5-speed (brand new)was about 11 seconds, so I read somewhere.  ||||reg||14
Z||000004||TheFiero64||10-31-2000||11:05 AM||||I disagree I love the Isuzu 5sp. I think it shifts smoother than the Getrag. There are a bunch of us v6 w/Isuzu 5's. I have 160,000 on my Isuzu and I drive it hard. It still runs like new. Please look at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002635.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/002635.html</A> <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
